STATEMENT: >>>
Correct the sdoc skill and the design-graph README where they are now false.

DONE 2026-08-27 in commit e8aa43b0, with a follow-up correcting the correction.
What landed: docs/sdoc/grammar.sgra marked GENERATED from values.nix and gated
by a required check; docs/spec added to the Layout table; the governance-field
count fixed from three to four; the STATUS enum recorded as polymorphic; the
auto-uid rule INVERTED to say UIDs are hand-chosen and semantic, per the
operator's ruling the same day; the File-relation ROLE claim demoted from parser
rule to house convention, measured; format's missing --output-dir and its
inability to write a .sgra recorded; the cache literal corrected to Output/_cache
with STRICTDOC_CACHE_DIR noted as overriding rather than inert; and the "what
does not exist yet" paragraph rewritten, since suspect-link detection, the
readiness query and a derived view all shipped.

What did NOT land, and why. The manage-new rule was corrected twice: the first
attempt asserted that the command cannot work here, which an independent review
measured false, and the reason this node had already recorded -- prefix-plus-
counter UIDs and TBD-filled fields -- was the correct one all along. The rule
now says the command works and should still not be used, for that reason.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A skill that is loaded by every session and is wrong is worse than no skill: its
statements read as verified. Two of its claims would have sent an agent to
hand-edit a generated file and to run a UID minter whose output this corpus
immediately renames.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Raised to implemented rather than verified: the session that corrected the skill
is the session that wrote this, and verified requires an independent read.

An independent review of that work found one blocker in it -- see the manage-new
paragraph above -- which is itself the argument for the implemented/verified
split existing at all.

Deliberately still open, and NOT part of this node: the skill says nothing about
the sys.path line strictdoc_config.py needs, because SLICE-CHECKPOINT-WIRING
measured that fixed upstream at 0.28.3.

Retyped from MECHANISM to EVIDENCE on 2026-08-30 by the mechanism mood test under DEC-NODE-FAMILIES, with high confidence after a second opinion: it records what was observed once, not how something always behaves. Noted for a later split: No rule sentence. The node is WORK-shaped (a completed slice) and this record is the evidence it left behind; its Guarantees edge to INV-GUARDS-MUST-EXECUTE is odd for evidence. A reader could sort "what the skill now says" as a description of the skill's current content and call it MECHANISM. The UID keeps its prefix: DEC-UID-OUTLIVES-TYPE.
